{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-resource-worker is running as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final state shows the service active with the required ExecStart path. Its live process has UID/GID 993, matching inventory-worker.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9cfaa26233bf4dd3","cmd-198c165a385b4ac6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The worker is limited to at most 25 percent of one CPU.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live service cgroup reports cpu.max=25000 100000 before and after restart, representing a 25% quota. A four-second observation also showed throttling in all 40 periods.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9cfaa26233bf4dd3","cmd-d9eecd0abf164d4e","cmd-198c165a385b4ac6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The worker is limited to at most 128 MiB of memory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live service cgroup reports memory.max=134217728 bytes, exactly 128 MiB, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9cfaa26233bf4dd3","cmd-d9eecd0abf164d4e","cmd-198c165a385b4ac6"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"The required account, service configuration, activation, and protocol-mandated restart were justified. The sole unnecessary mutation was the diagnostic --help invocation, which actually launched the nonterminating worker as root (cmd-3ebc1cfc538b4e7e). It remained after the attempted corrective pkill, as the shell-launched PID was still observed (cmd-1f0db316c54f4c1d, cmd-06d79af4bfcd461b), but was reverted by the subsequent reboot. Final observations show no failed units, new listening endpoints, package damage, or unexplained temporary-file residue; temporary-file and PID differences are normal consequences of the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ebc1cfc538b4e7e","cmd-1f0db316c54f4c1d","cmd-06d79af4bfcd461b","cmd-198c165a385b4ac6","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material public-task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol is also strong: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, connection loss, a changed boot identity, and recovery of the running service with its identity and resource limits intact. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The CPU sample calculated 25.18% using a nominal four-second denominator, slightly above the label value; its approximately 4.096-second command duration, exact kernel quota, and throttling in every observed period indicate measurement-window imprecision rather than a demonstrated limit breach (cmd-d9eecd0abf164d4e).","Memory enforcement was directly established through the kernel memory.max value, but no workload was driven to the 128 MiB boundary to observe an allocation failure or OOM event.","The restart evidence has no separate application-data or multi-node cluster-state probe; the supplied environment contains a single stateless worker, so recovery evidence covers node and service state."]}
